{
  "abstract": "Let P be a finite polyhedral space with compatible simplex charts of constant curvature κ ∈ {−1,0,1}, let d be the chart dimension, and let n ≥ d. Every short map from P to the corresponding n-dimensional model should admit a uniformly close PL-isometry. In the spherical case the Challenge additionally assumes uniform strict shortness or that the image lies in an open hemisphere.",
